cluding Meghan Miller and Louis Moresi from ANU analysed datasets from over 300 seismic stations.","date":"2020-07-24","thumbnail":"/banner-8bce4891ccdc745f5ba998bb694c23cd.png","thumbnailOptimized":"","banner":"/banner-8bce4891ccdc745f5ba998bb694c23cd.png","bannerOptimized":"","tags":[],"level":3},{"slug":"australian-cities-are-quiet-during-lockdown-earthquake-scientists-are-making-the-most-of-it","title":"Australian cities are quiet during lockdown. Earthquake scientists are making the most of it","description":"Meghan S. Miller (ANU) Louis Moresi (ANU) Our responses to the COVID-19 pandemic have dramatically changed human activity all over the world. Sensitive instruments are detecting far less of the noise and vibration produced by humans in motion.","date":"2020-07-17","thumbnail":"/banner-89f4687bdbdd85f638e2fa4953ee1785.png","thumbnailOptimized":"","banner":"/banner-89f4687bdbdd85f638e2fa4953ee1785.png","bannerOptimized":"","tags":[],"level":3},{"slug":"self-updating-repositories","title":"Australian Seismometers in Schools - Noise monitoring dashboard","description":"How we built a simple dashboard using Github actions with open source software and openly available (FAIR) data.","date":"2020-07-17","thumbnail":"/banner-c7961006537c47ec76ed4f3f2960775a.png","thumbnailOptimized":"","banner":"/banner-c7961006537c47ec76ed4f3f2960775a.png","bannerOptimized":"","tags":[],"level":3},{"slug":"publication-news","title":"Underworld publication news: Crustal thickness anomalies in stable continents.","description":"","date":"2020-07-09","thumbnail":"/badge_logo-9873eb9db8d49e5fc6c9d98f2182b353.svg","thumbnailOptimized":"","banner":"","bannerOptimized":"","tags":[],"level":3},{"slug":"underworld-2-9","title":"Underworld 2.9","description":"The Underworld 2.9 release is available from Github, as a docker container and via zenodo (doi:10.5281/zenodo.3964957) it is also available through pip install for the first time","date":"2020-04-03","thumbnail":"/banner-b1ed1570c13c7